-- הוראת תכ"ם 13.4.2 "תשלום קצובת נסיעה", מהדורה 6 (17.11.2022)
-- The Accountant-General's instruction on the travel allowance of government
-- employees, rewritten for the "Derech Shava" public-transport reform of
-- 1.8.2022: who is entitled and who is not, a partial month, a partial use
-- of a government vehicle, the hourly employee, the blind employee, a
-- locality without public transport, Sabbath and holiday travel, reporting
-- an address, and payment through the payroll. Editions 7 to 11 import this
-- file where they repeat it.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT parties
IMPORT `kitzuvat-nesia-common`
IMPORT `taarifei-nesia-common`
IMPORT `taarifei-nesia-in-force-common`

-- Every tariff is the notice's "לוח תעריפי נסיעה בתחבורה ציבורית" (HOD
-- 13.4.2.1): `travel fares`, read off the notice in force by `the travel
-- allowance on the route` below. Agorot: the edition sets no rounding,
-- so by convention rounding.default no rule here rounds.

-- not weighed against `the Equal Pay Law`: ‘בעל’ here is the holder of a
-- post or of a service or assigned car (‘בעל רכב צמוד’, ‘בעל נהג צמוד’),
-- not a husband; the instruction sets one travel allowance for every
-- employee, man or woman, and does not distinguish between them.

-- not weighed against `the Advance Notice Law`: ‘חודש סיום העסקה’ here is a
-- month in which the travel allowance is paid pro rata (2.1.4), not notice
-- of dismissal or resignation.

§ `הוראת תכ"ם 13.4.2 תשלום קצובת נסיעה — מהדורה 6`

§§ `1 מבוא`

-- 1.1: the employees of the government ministries and their auxiliary
-- units are refunded the travel allowance by public transport, by the rules
-- of this instruction.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_1__subpara_1-1
GIVEN `employed by a government ministry or an auxiliary unit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `edition 6 applies to` `employed by a government ministry or an auxiliary unit` IF
    `employed by a government ministry or an auxiliary unit`

-- akn:hc_1__para_1__subpara_1-2 Further payments where the permanent workplace is in Eilat or the Negev, or for official travel to Eilat, are the notice "תשלומים לנוסעים / עובדים באילת ותוספת ערבה", which the corpus does not hold; no rule here.
-- akn:hc_1__para_1__subpara_1-3 akn:hc_1__para_1__subpara_1-3/p2 The instruction's purpose, to direct the ministries on the refund; no rule.
-- akn:hc_1__para_1__subpara_1-4 A pointer to annex A, whose definitions the rules below cite; no rule.

§§ `2.1 זכאות לקצובת נסיעה`

-- akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-1 The heading "זכאות לקצובת נסיעה"; its clauses follow.

-- 2.1.1 and annex A's definition 6: an employee who needs transport from
-- the residence to the workplace, by public transport, a private car or
-- any other means, is entitled to the travel allowance, a refund of the
-- actual expense of travel from the residence to the workplace, at the
-- notice's tariffs; 2.2 takes out those who are not.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-1__cls_2-1-1 akn:att_1__hc_1__para_6
GIVEN m IS A `travel month`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `entitled to the travel allowance, edition 6` m IF
        m's `needs transport from home to work`
    AND NOT `not entitled under 2.2, edition 6` m

-- 2.1.2 and annex A's definition 4: from one residence only, the address
-- where the employee lives most days of the week, by the employee's
-- declaration.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-1__cls_2-1-2 akn:att_1__hc_1__para_4
`the residences the allowance is paid from, edition 6` MEANS 1

-- 2.1.3: the refund does not depend on how often the transport runs or on
-- when the employee's work starts or ends.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-1__cls_2-1-3
`the refund depends on the frequency of transport or the hours of work, edition 6` MEANS FALSE

-- 2.1.4 and annex A's definitions 2-3: in a month not fully worked (the
-- month employment starts or ends, unpaid leave) the allowance is the lower
-- of the monthly ticket "חופשי חודשי - אוטובוס + רכבת" (a calendar month,
-- the 1st to the month's end) and the daily ticket "חופשי יומי - אוטובוס +
-- רכבת" (valid the day it is bought) times the days actually worked. The
-- monthly allowance of a full month is the monthly ticket: 2.1.1 sends it to
-- the notice, and 2.1.4.1 names it.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-1__cls_2-1-4 akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-1__cls_2-1-4__pnt_2-1-4-1 akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-1__cls_2-1-4__pnt_2-1-4-2 akn:att_1__hc_1__para_2 akn:att_1__hc_1__para_3
GIVEN f IS A `travel fares`, m IS A `travel month`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the monthly employee's allowance, edition 6` f m IS
    IF m's `a full month of work`
    THEN f's `monthly free pass`
    ELSE `the lower of the monthly pass and the daily passes` f m

-- 2.1.5: an employee who travels part of the month in a government vehicle
-- or by another arrangement the Treasury funds gets a partial allowance, in
-- proportion to the trips made otherwise.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-1__cls_2-1-5
GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER, m IS A `travel month`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the partial allowance for a partial State-funded month, edition 6` amount m IS
    `in proportion to the trips not State-funded` amount m

§§ `2.2 אי זכאות לקצובת נסיעה`

-- 2.2.1 and its four cases, with annex A's definition 1 (a calendar month,
-- from its 1st to its last day): not entitled is an employee who travels to
-- or from work in a government vehicle or another Treasury-funded
-- arrangement (shuttles included), has an assigned car, has an assigned
-- driver, or is absent an unbroken calendar month or more. The first case
-- takes out the employee who travels so all month; part of the month is
-- 2.1.5's.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-2 akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-2__cls_2-2-1 akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-2__cls_2-2-1__pnt_2-2-1-1 akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-2__cls_2-2-1__pnt_2-2-1-2 akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-2__cls_2-2-1__pnt_2-2-1-3 akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-2__cls_2-2-1__pnt_2-2-1-4 akn:att_1__hc_1__para_1
GIVEN m IS A `travel month`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `not entitled under 2.2, edition 6` m IF
        m's `share of trips by a State-funded arrangement` AT LEAST 1
    OR  m's `has an assigned car`
    OR  m's `has an assigned driver`
    OR  m's `absent a calendar month or more`

§§ `2.3 קביעת זכאות לקצובת נסיעה בעקבות רפורמת דרך שווה`

-- akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-3 The heading; its clauses follow.

-- 2.3.1: from 1.8.2022 the "Derech Shava" reform sets the tariffs by the
-- distance between origin and destination and the means (bus, or bus and
-- train); it was decided that employees are refunded for every means of
-- public transport, the train included. 2.3.2: the entitlement follows the
-- notice's rules.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-3__cls_2-3-1 akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-3__cls_2-3-2
`the train is refunded with every other means of public transport, edition 6` MEANS TRUE

-- 2.3.3: the travel-allowance equalisation for those taken into the State
-- service by 31.7.2022 is the notice's; its amount is an input.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-3__cls_2-3-3
GIVEN m IS A `travel month`, `the equalisation the notice sets` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the travel-allowance equalisation, edition 6` m `the equalisation the notice sets` IS
    IF m's `taken into the State service by 31.7.2022`
    THEN `the equalisation the notice sets`
    ELSE 0

-- 2.3.4: an hourly employee is paid the daily tickets "חופשי יומי -
-- אוטובוס + רכבת" for the days travelled to work, but no more than the
-- monthly ticket.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-3__cls_2-3-4 akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-3__cls_2-3-4__pnt_2-3-4-1
GIVEN f IS A `travel fares`, m IS A `travel month`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the hourly employee's allowance, edition 6` f m IS
    `the lower of the monthly pass and the daily passes` f m

-- The monthly allowance before the blind rule, the Sabbath and the
-- locality supplement.
GIVEN f IS A `travel fares`, m IS A `travel month`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the allowance for travel to work, edition 6` f m IS
    `the partial allowance for a partial State-funded month, edition 6`
        (IF m's `kind of employee` EQUALS `an employee paid by the hour`
         THEN `the hourly employee's allowance, edition 6` f m
         ELSE `the monthly employee's allowance, edition 6` f m)
        m

-- 2.3.5 and annex A's definition 5: a blind employee (one holding a blind
-- person's certificate, a copy filed with human resources and the salary
-- unit) is paid five times the monthly ticket "חופשי חודשי - אוטובוס +
-- רכבת", and that entitlement cancels every other in the instruction.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-3__cls_2-3-5 akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-3__cls_2-3-5__pnt_2-3-5-1 akn:att_1__hc_1__para_5
GIVEN f IS A `travel fares`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the blind employee's allowance, edition 6` f IS
    5 TIMES f's `monthly free pass`

-- 2.3.6: an employee living in a locality without public transport who
-- uses another means to reach the main road on the way to work is entitled,
-- in addition to the allowance, to 128 shekels a month (code 901).
@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-3__cls_2-3-6 akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-3__cls_2-3-6__pnt_2-3-6-1
GIVEN m IS A `travel month`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the supplement for a locality without public transport, edition 6` m IS
    IF m's `lives where there is no public transport` THEN 128 ELSE 0

§§ `2.4 קצובה בגין נסיעה בשבתות וחגים`

-- akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-4 The heading; its clauses follow.

-- 2.4.1-2.4.2: an employee who starts or ends work after the Sabbath or a
-- holiday with no public transport has come in is paid the daily ticket
-- "חופשי יומי - אוטובוס + רכבת" for the trip from home to work and back,
-- only for the Sabbath and holiday days the employee actually came to work.
-- Not for an employee with a service or personal car, nor in an office with
-- a shuttle arrangement.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-4__cls_2-4-1 akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-4__cls_2-4-2
GIVEN f IS A `travel fares`, m IS A `travel month`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the Sabbath and holiday allowance, edition 6` f m IS
    IF m's `has a service or personal car` OR m's `the office runs a shuttle`
    THEN 0
    ELSE f's `daily free pass` TIMES m's `Sabbath and holiday days reached`

-- 2.4.3: the Sabbath refund and the monthly allowance together may not
-- exceed "the payment cap, as in section 2.3 above"; section 2.3 states no
-- cap, and neither does any other clause of the edition
-- (F-2022-11-17_takam_H-13-4-2_kitzuvat-nesia_v6-a). The reading adopted:
-- the cap is an input of this edition, `the payment cap 2.4.3 refers to`.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-4__cls_2-4-3
GIVEN f IS A `travel fares`, m IS A `travel month`, `the payment cap 2.4.3 refers to` IS A NUMBER @desc the cap 2.4.3 sends to section 2.3, which states none
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the allowance within the payment cap, edition 6` f m `the payment cap 2.4.3 refers to` IS
    min (`the allowance for travel to work, edition 6` f m PLUS `the Sabbath and holiday allowance, edition 6` f m)
        `the payment cap 2.4.3 refers to`

-- The caps section 2.3 states, for 2.4.3 to refer to: none.
`the caps section 2.3 states, edition 6` MEANS EMPTY

`section 2.4.3 refers to a cap section 2.3 does not state, edition 6` MEANS
    `the caps section 2.3 states, edition 6` EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `section 2.4.3 refers to a cap section 2.3 does not state, edition 6`

`why 2.4.3 gives no figure for the cap, edition 6` MEANS
    `the text is silent` "F-2022-11-17_takam_H-13-4-2_kitzuvat-nesia_v6-a"

-- The month's travel allowance: none where 2.2 takes the employee out; the
-- blind employee's in place of every other (2.3.5); otherwise the allowance
-- with the Sabbath days, within the cap, and the locality supplement "in
-- addition". The equalisation of 2.3.3 is the notice's and is not added
-- here.
GIVEN f IS A `travel fares`, m IS A `travel month`, `the payment cap 2.4.3 refers to` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the travel allowance, edition 6` f m `the payment cap 2.4.3 refers to` IS
    BRANCH IF NOT `entitled to the travel allowance, edition 6` m THEN 0
           IF m's `blind` THEN `the blind employee's allowance, edition 6` f
           OTHERWISE `the allowance within the payment cap, edition 6` f m `the payment cap 2.4.3 refers to`
                     PLUS `the supplement for a locality without public transport, edition 6` m

§§ `2.5 דיווח על כתובת מגורים`

-- akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-5 The heading; its clauses follow.

-- 2.5.1 and 2.5.3: an employee who changed residence or workplace reports
-- it to the office's human resources on the form "קצובת נסיעה"; human
-- resources pass the report to the salary unit, which pays the updated
-- allowance. One who did not report it in writing has every payment
-- difference collected retroactively from the day of the move. The edition
-- sets no time limit.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-5__cls_2-5-1 akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-5__cls_2-5-3
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `travel-allowance duty`
DECIDE `reporting a move, edition 6` IS
    PARTY `the government employee`
    MUST  `report the new address or workplace on the travel-allowance form`
    HENCE (PARTY `the employer`
           MUST  `pass the report to the salary unit`
           HENCE (PARTY `the employer`
                  MUST  `pay the updated travel allowance`))
    LEST  (PARTY `the employer`
           MAY   `collect the payment differences retroactively`)

-- 2.5.2: the employee refreshes the details at least once in 3 years, on
-- the same form; the payment is blocked in the payroll until it is done.
-- Time is counted in months.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-5__cls_2-5-2
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `travel-allowance duty`
DECIDE `refreshing the details, edition 6` IS
    PARTY `the government employee`
    MUST  `refresh the travel-allowance details`
    WITHIN 36
    LEST  (PARTY `the employer`
           MAY   `block the travel allowance in the payroll`)

§§ `2.6 יישום במערכות השכר`

-- akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-6 The heading; its clauses follow.

-- 2.6.1 and annex B §1: the allowance is paid through the payroll, by the
-- notice's directions and annex B's codes. 2.6.2: an accountancy whose
-- salaries are not computed in "Malam Sachar" pays by the instruction's
-- rules.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-6__cls_2-6-1 akn:att_2__hc_1__para_1
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `travel-allowance duty`
DECIDE `paying through the payroll, edition 6` IS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `pay the travel allowance through the payroll`

@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-6__cls_2-6-2
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `travel-allowance duty`
DECIDE `paying outside Malam, edition 6` IS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `pay the travel allowance by the instruction's rules outside Malam`

§§ `3-4 מסמכים ישימים ונספחים`

-- akn:hc_1__para_3__subpara_3-1 akn:hc_1__para_3__subpara_3-2 akn:hc_1__para_3__subpara_3-3 akn:hc_1__para_3__subpara_3-4 akn:hc_1__para_3__subpara_3-5 The applicable documents (the takshir's chapters 28.3 and 28.37, the form, the two notices); a source list, no rule.
-- akn:hc_1__para_4__subpara_4-1 akn:hc_1__para_4__subpara_4-2 akn:hc_1__para_4__subpara_4-3 The list of annexes; no rule.
-- akn:att_1__hc_1/p1 Annex A's title "הגדרות"; its definitions are cited by the rules that use them.
-- akn:att_2__hc_1/p1 Annex B's title; its clauses follow.
-- akn:att_2__hc_1__para_2 akn:att_2__hc_1__para_2/t1 The payroll codes each kind of payment is reported under in "Malam Sachar" (0811, event 226 code 4820, 0971, 901, 1077); payroll coding, no entitlement of its own.
-- akn:att_2__hc_1__para_3 The codes of the public-transport lines are the notice's; a pointer, no rule.
-- akn:att_3__hc_1/p1 akn:att_3__hc_1/p2 akn:att_3__hc_1/t1 Annex C, the table of the editions' changes; a record, no rule.

§§ `התעריפים — the notice in force`

-- The edition reads the monthly free pass and the daily free pass; here they are read off the notice
-- "לוח תעריפי נסיעה בתחבורה ציבורית" in force on the month's day (HOD
-- 13.4.2.1, `taarifei-nesia-in-force-common`), for the employee's route. Where
-- the notice prints no tariff the edition reads, there is no answer.
GIVEN r IS A `travel route`, d IS A DATE @desc the month's day
      m IS A `travel month`
      `the payment cap 2.4.3 refers to` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the travel allowance on the route, edition 6` r d m `the payment cap 2.4.3 refers to` IS
    CONSIDER `the travel fares of the route on` r d TRUE FALSE FALSE
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST f THEN JUST (`the travel allowance, edition 6` f m `the payment cap 2.4.3 refers to`)

-- The equalisation supplement the notice in force sets, on the route's
-- monthly free pass.
GIVEN r IS A `travel route`, d IS A DATE
      m IS A `travel month`
      x IS A NUMBER @desc the allowance paid before the reform, every component included
      `the highest allowance of 2022` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the travel-allowance equalisation on the route, edition 6` r d m x `the highest allowance of 2022` IS
    CONSIDER `the tariffs of the route on` r d
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST rt THEN
        CONSIDER rt's `route monthly pass`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST monthly THEN
            CONSIDER `the equalisation supplement in force on` d x monthly `the highest allowance of 2022`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST s THEN JUST (`the travel-allowance equalisation, edition 6` m s)

§§ `Worked examples`

-- The tariffs are placeholders, round figures; the notice's own are read by
-- `the travel allowance on the route, edition 6` (last example).
`placeholder fares, edition 6` MEANS
    `travel fares` WITH
        `monthly free pass`     IS 300
        `daily free pass`       IS 20
        `single fare`           IS 10
        `intercity single fare` IS 0

`a monthly employee's month, edition 6` MEANS `an ordinary travel month` `a monthly employee` 22

`edition 6 pays` m MEANS `the travel allowance, edition 6` `placeholder fares, edition 6` m 1330

#ASSERT `edition 6 pays` `a monthly employee's month, edition 6` EQUALS 300

-- 2.1.4: a month of 10 days worked, the lower of 300 and 10 x 20.
`a partial month of 10 days, edition 6` MEANS
    `the travel month changed` (`an ordinary travel month` `a monthly employee` 10) FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE 0 0
#ASSERT `edition 6 pays` `a partial month of 10 days, edition 6` EQUALS 200

-- 2.3.4: an hourly employee's 22 days cost more than the monthly ticket;
-- 10 days cost less.
#ASSERT `edition 6 pays` (`an ordinary travel month` `an employee paid by the hour` 22) EQUALS 300
#ASSERT `edition 6 pays` (`an ordinary travel month` `an employee paid by the hour` 10) EQUALS 200

-- 2.1.5: half the trips by a government vehicle.
`a month half by a government vehicle, edition 6` MEANS
    `the travel month changed` `a monthly employee's month, edition 6` TRUE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE 0 0.5
#ASSERT `edition 6 pays` `a month half by a government vehicle, edition 6` EQUALS 150

-- 2.3.5: five monthly tickets, in place of everything else.
`a blind employee's month with Sabbaths and no public transport, edition 6` MEANS
    `the travel month changed` `a monthly employee's month, edition 6` TRUE TRUE 4 TRUE FALSE 0 0
#ASSERT `edition 6 pays` `a blind employee's month with Sabbaths and no public transport, edition 6` EQUALS 1500

-- 2.3.6 and 2.4: a locality without public transport and four Sabbath days.
`a month with Sabbaths and no public transport, edition 6` MEANS
    `the travel month changed` `a monthly employee's month, edition 6` TRUE FALSE 4 TRUE FALSE 0 0
#ASSERT `edition 6 pays` `a month with Sabbaths and no public transport, edition 6` EQUALS 508

-- 2.2: an employee who travels the whole month by a State arrangement.
`a month all by a government vehicle, edition 6` MEANS
    `the travel month changed` `a monthly employee's month, edition 6` TRUE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE 0 1
#ASSERT `edition 6 pays` `a month all by a government vehicle, edition 6` EQUALS 0

-- On 1.12.2022, a monthly employee of 22 days on `a 30 km route` (the
-- Tel Aviv codes before the reform, 30 km by bus after it): the edition's
-- allowance on the tariffs the notice in force prints.
#ASSERT `the travel allowance on the route, edition 6` `a 30 km route` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 12 2022) (`an ordinary travel month` `a monthly employee` 22) 1330 EQUALS
    JUST (`the travel allowance, edition 6` `the route's fares on 1.12.2022, edition 6` (`an ordinary travel month` `a monthly employee` 22) 1330)

`the route's fares on 1.12.2022, edition 6` MEANS
    `travel fares` WITH
        `monthly free pass`     IS 255
        `daily free pass`       IS 28
        `single fare`           IS 0
        `intercity single fare` IS 0
